## Contract
Enumerate genomic sites in GRCh38 where an ASO's target (reverse complement) matches the pre-mRNA-sense strand with <=K substitutions (K default 0..3; edit-distance optional, off by default). Search space = pre-mRNA gene bodies (exons AND introns) from GENCODE v50 GTF (~/orcd/scratch/feng/gencode/v50/gencode.v50.primary_assembly.annotation.gtf; read gene lines only via bounded awk/py) on the correct gene strand — state explicitly which regions the index includes; do not reuse the exonic-union notion. 
Output record per site: aso_id, chrom, start1,end1 (1-based inclusive), gene strand, gene_id, region class (exon/intron/junction-spanning/UTR as derivable), mismatch count + mismatch positions (ASO 5'->3'), target seq, evidence_class (derived), paralog_ambiguity flag (SMN1/SMN2 sequence-identical sites must both appear with distinct site IDs and ambiguity flag), duplicate policy documented (same coords across overlapping transcripts of one gene collapse to one site with transcript list).
Deterministic sharding by (chrom, window) with stable shard IDs; atomic tmp->rename parquet + .done manifest (rows, sha256, params, fasta/gtf identity); idempotent restart.
Tests: brute-force oracle on tiny synthetic references (random, with planted exact/mismatched/reverse-strand sites, overlapping hits, N bases, chrom edges) must equal seed-extend results exactly; strand correctness for + and - genes; off-by-one; shard union == unsharded; restart idempotence; F18/F14/F10 exact hits include SMN2 ISS-N1 site chr5:70076584-70076601 and SMN1 paralog site (reference F1 module for coords).
Sentinel: jobs/j6_sentinel.sbatch (partition mit_quicktest, <=10 min, --requeue) over a small bounded region (chr5:70.0-71.1 Mb) for F18/F14/F10; DO NOT submit it, just make it ready; report the exact command.
